 of Stanniocalcin 2 as Prognostic Marker in Renal Cell Carcinoma</article-title><source>Eur Urol</source><comment></comment></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kristiansen</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Pilarsky</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Wissmann</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Kaiser</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Bruemmendorf</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Roepcke</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Dahl</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Hinzmann</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Specht</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Pervan</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><etal></etal></person-group><article-title>Expression profiling of microdissected matched prostate cancer samples reveals CD166/MEMD and CD24 as new prognostic markers for patient survival</article-title><source>J Pathol</source><year>2005</year><volume>205</volume><fpage>359</fpage><lpage>376</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15532095</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/path.1676</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dhanasekaran</surname><given-names>SM</given-names></name><name><surname>Barrette</surname><given-names>TR</given-names></name><name><surname>Ghosh</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Shah</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Varambally</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Kurachi</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Pienta</surname><given-names>KJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Rubin</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Chinnaiyan</surname><given-names>A